{
 "thread": "M053M3FC4B4",
 "subject": "extract regression output from coplots",
 "messages_listed": 3,
 "last_activity": "2015-12-04T19:30:10Z",
 "messages": [
  {
   "id": "bvMWhvztCAAJ",
   "from": "Alex Webster",
   "author": "eca599486d272d65",
   "date": "2015-12-04T00:08:38Z",
   "subject": "extract regression output from coplots",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">I find coplots a super useful visual tool for interpreting interactions in mixed models, but sometimes I&#39;d like to also see the breakdown in numbers so that I can compare intercepts, etc and know the exact bins of the &quot;Given&quot; variable that R is magically choosing. Does anyone know how to extract the regression output from coplots?<div><br><div>for example, this code below gives me the attached plot. I&#39;d be down to see the regression output for simple linear regressions if that&#39;s all I can get, or for the full mixed models at these different levels of the &quot;Given&quot; variable if possible. I realize that I could code the model for each of these different levels, but I&#39;d rather see what the coplot is doing and have them line up exactly. And it would be faster if there is just a line of code for this. Can&#39;t find anything via google, though others have asked the question, to no avail. Let me know what you think - Thanks!</div><div><br></div><div>coplot(log_DEA ~ daub_veg_H1_total_veg_cover | Fore_slope_ammended, rows=1, panel=panel.car, lowess.line=FALSE, data=DEAslope)<br></div><div><br></div><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"><a href=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-0yyz5iT4_5U/VmDXop_xOuI/AAAAAAAAPWs/IsQy7vvvJ68/s1600/Rplot.png\" style=\"margin-left:1em;margin-right:1em\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-0yyz5iT4_5U/VmDXop_xOuI/AAAAAAAAPWs/IsQy7vvvJ68/s1600/Rplot.png&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792467659994000&amp;usg=AOvVaw15-uCeQdN0hAXeSENJ0nMb\"><img src=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-0yyz5iT4_5U/VmDXop_xOuI/AAAAAAAAPWs/IsQy7vvvJ68/s320/Rplot.png\" border=\"0\" width=\"320\" height=\"267\"></a></p></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "Gzli81IpCQAJ",
   "from": "Matt Whalen",
   "author": "4742ff1f9fc5f9ca",
   "date": "2015-12-04T18:16:00Z",
   "subject": "Re: [D-RUG]: extract regression output from coplots",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hey Alex,<div><br></div><div>Looks like<font face=\"monospace, monospace\"> coplot() </font>splits your conditional variable (fore_slope_ammended) into some arbitrary number of intervals that have some arbitrary amount of overlap. This is what function <font face=\"monospace, monospace\">co.intervals() </font>does, and the default for continuous conditional variables is to generate 6 intervals that overlap by 50% (see the help page for <font face=\"monospace, monospace\">coplot</font>)...in your plot, some of the data points in the different panels are the same. Once the intervals have been calculated, <font face=\"monospace, monospace\">panel.car()</font> plots the data points and optional linear regressions and loess smoothers. I am assuming that the function generates 6 data.frames that are subsets of the full dataset containing the data that falls into each interval for fore_slope_ammended, and then <font face=\"monospace, monospace\">panel.car</font> runs separate regressions (so, no full model with interactions and no mixed models).</div><div><br></div><div>The point of this whole thing seems to be visualizing statistical interactions. In this particular case, there does not seem to be much evidence for an interaction (the slopes are intercepts are qualitatively similar to my eye). Perhaps some of your other variables do show interactions, in which case it would be good to run models with statistical interactions (e.g. <span style=\"font-size:12.8px\"><font face=\"monospace, monospace\">lm(log_DEA ~ daub_veg_H1_total_veg_cover * Fore_slope_ammended) </font>)</span></div><div><br></div><div>I doubt there is an easy way to pull of the regression statistics using <font face=\"monospace, monospace\">coplot</font>. However, you should be able to use <font face=\"monospace, monospace\">co.intervals</font> and then run linear models on your own.</div><div><br></div><div>Here is an example using the quakes dataset (the one used in the help file for <font face=\"monospace, monospace\">coplot</font>):</div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px;line-height:20px\"><h1 style=\"margin:20px 0px 10px;font-size:36px;font-family:inherit;font-weight:500;line-height:1.1;color:inherit\">Quakes coplot example</h1></div><pre style=\"overflow:auto;font-size:13px;padding:9.5px;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:10px;line-height:1.42857;color:rgb(51,51,51);word-wrap:break-word;border:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);border-radius:4px;background-color:rgb(245,245,245)\"><code style=\"font-size:inherit;padding-top:0px;padding-right:0px;padding-left:0px;color:inherit;border-radius:0px;white-space:pre-wrap;background-color:transparent\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">coplot</span><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">(</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">lat</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">~</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">long</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">|</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">depth</span>, <span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">data</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">=</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">quakes</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">)</span></code></pre><p style=\"margin:0px 0px 10px;color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px;line-height:20px\"><img src=\"https://groups.google.com/group/davis-rug/attach/92952f362391b/image.png?part=0.2&amp;view=1\" alt=\"Inline image 4\" width=\"470\" height=\"336\"></p><p style=\"margin:0px 0px 10px;color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px;line-height:20px\">What are the intervals being used?</p><pre style=\"overflow:auto;font-size:13px;padding:9.5px;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:10px;line-height:1.42857;color:rgb(51,51,51);word-wrap:break-word;border:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);border-radius:4px;background-color:rgb(245,245,245)\"><code style=\"font-size:inherit;padding-top:0px;padding-right:0px;padding-left:0px;color:inherit;border-radius:0px;white-space:pre-wrap;background-color:transparent\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">with</span><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">(</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">quakes</span>, <span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">co.intervals</span><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">depth</span><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">)</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">)</span>   <span style=\"color:rgb(153,153,136);font-style:italic\"># using defaults, 6 intervals with 50% overlap</span></code></pre><pre style=\"overflow:auto;font-size:13px;padding:9.5px;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:10px;line-height:1.42857;color:rgb(51,51,51);word-wrap:break-word;border:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);border-radius:4px\"><code style=\"font-size:inherit;padding:0px;color:inherit;border-radius:0px;white-space:pre-wrap;background-color:transparent\">##       [,1]  [,2]\r\n## [1,]  39.5 118.5\r\n## [2,]  64.5 204.5\r\n## [3,] 117.5 343.5\r\n## [4,] 203.5 526.5\r\n## [5,] 347.5 584.5\r\n## [6,] 526.5 680.5</code></pre><p style=\"margin:0px 0px 10px;color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px;line-height:20px\">Save the intervals, use them to subset the quakes data.frame</p><pre style=\"overflow:auto;font-size:13px;padding:9.5px;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:10px;line-height:1.42857;color:rgb(51,51,51);word-wrap:break-word;border:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);border-radius:4px;background-color:rgb(245,245,245)\"><code style=\"font-size:inherit;padding-top:0px;padding-right:0px;padding-left:0px;color:inherit;border-radius:0px;white-space:pre-wrap;background-color:transparent\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">int</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">&lt;-</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">with</span><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">(</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">quakes</span>, <span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">co.intervals</span><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">depth</span><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">)</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">)</span>  \r\n<span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><a href=\"http://quake.int\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://quake.int&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792467660000000&amp;usg=AOvVaw20on7OdK_vDq-tt35E9z7R\">quake.int</a></span> <span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">&lt;-</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">list</span><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">)</span>\r\n<span style=\"color:rgb(153,0,0);font-weight:bold\">for</span><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">i</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(153,0,0);font-weight:bold\">in</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(0,153,153)\">1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">:</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">nrow</span><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">int</span><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">)</span><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">)</span><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">{</span>\r\n     <span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><a href=\"http://quake.int\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://quake.int&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792467660000000&amp;usg=AOvVaw20on7OdK_vDq-tt35E9z7R\">quake.int</a></span><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">[</span><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">[</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">i</span><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">]</span><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">]</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">&lt;-</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">quakes</span><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">[</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">quakes</span><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">$</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">depth</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">&gt;=</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">int</span><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">[</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">i</span>,<span style=\"color:rgb(0,153,153)\">1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">]</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">&amp;</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">quakes</span><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">$</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">depth</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">&lt;=</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">int</span><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">[</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">i</span>,<span style=\"color:rgb(0,153,153)\">2</span><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">]</span>,<span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">]</span>\r\n     <span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">}</span></code></pre><p style=\"margin:0px 0px 10px;color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px;line-height:20px\">Generate linear models – note, there are functions to do this (e.g. lmList in package nlme)</p><pre style=\"overflow:auto;font-size:13px;padding:9.5px;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:10px;line-height:1.42857;color:rgb(51,51,51);word-wrap:break-word;border:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);border-radius:4px;background-color:rgb(245,245,245)\"><code style=\"font-size:inherit;padding-top:0px;padding-right:0px;padding-left:0px;color:inherit;border-radius:0px;white-space:pre-wrap;background-color:transparent\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><a href=\"http://lm.int\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://lm.int&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792467660000000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2jywar5vBwiGipli3tWaeB\">lm.int</a></span> <span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">&lt;-</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">list</span><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">)</span>\r\n<span style=\"color:rgb(153,0,0);font-weight:bold\">for</span><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">i</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(153,0,0);font-weight:bold\">in</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(0,153,153)\">1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">:</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">nrow</span><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">int</span><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">)</span><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">)</span><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">{</span>\r\n     <span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><a href=\"http://lm.int\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://lm.int&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792467660000000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2jywar5vBwiGipli3tWaeB\">lm.int</a></span><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">[</span><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">[</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">i</span><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">]</span><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">]</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">&lt;-</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">lm</span><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">(</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">lat</span><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">~</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">long</span>, <span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">data</span><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><a href=\"http://quake.int\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://quake.int&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792467660000000&amp;usg=AOvVaw20on7OdK_vDq-tt35E9z7R\">quake.int</a></span><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">[</span><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">[</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">i</span><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">]</span><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">]</span><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">)</span>\r\n     <span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">}</span></code></pre><p style=\"margin:0px 0px 10px;color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px;line-height:20px\">Plot the data and add regression lines</p><pre style=\"overflow:auto;font-size:13px;padding:9.5px;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:10px;line-height:1.42857;color:rgb(51,51,51);word-wrap:break-word;border:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);border-radius:4px;background-color:rgb(245,245,245)\"><code style=\"font-size:inherit;padding-top:0px;padding-right:0px;padding-left:0px;color:inherit;border-radius:0px;white-space:pre-wrap;background-color:transparent\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">par</span><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">mfrow</span><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">c</span><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,153,153)\">2</span>,<span style=\"color:rgb(0,153,153)\">3</span><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">)</span><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">)</span>\r\n<span style=\"color:rgb(153,0,0);font-weight:bold\">for</span><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">i</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(153,0,0);font-weight:bold\">in</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(0,153,153)\">1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">:</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">nrow</span><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">int</span><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">)</span><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">)</span><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">{</span>\r\n     <span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">plot</span><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">(</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">lat</span><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">~</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">long</span>, <span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><a href=\"http://quake.int\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://quake.int&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792467660000000&amp;usg=AOvVaw20on7OdK_vDq-tt35E9z7R\">quake.int</a></span><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">[</span><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">[</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">i</span><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">]</span><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">]</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">)</span>\r\n     <span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">abline</span><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">(</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><a href=\"http://lm.int\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://lm.int&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792467660000000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2jywar5vBwiGipli3tWaeB\">lm.int</a></span><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">[</span><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">[</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">i</span><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">]</span><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">]</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">)</span>\r\n     <span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">}</span></code></pre><p style=\"margin:0px 0px 10px;color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px;line-height:20px\"><img src=\"https://groups.google.com/group/davis-rug/attach/92952f362391b/image.png?part=0.1&amp;view=1\" alt=\"Inline image 3\" width=\"470\" height=\"336\"></p><p style=\"margin:0px 0px 10px;color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px;line-height:20px\">Pull regression coefficients into a matrix</p><pre style=\"overflow:auto;font-size:13px;padding:9.5px;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:10px;line-height:1.42857;color:rgb(51,51,51);word-wrap:break-word;border:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);border-radius:4px;background-color:rgb(245,245,245)\"><code style=\"font-size:inherit;padding-top:0px;padding-right:0px;padding-left:0px;color:inherit;border-radius:0px;white-space:pre-wrap;background-color:transparent\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">matrix</span><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">(</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">unlist</span><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">(</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">lapply</span><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">(</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><a href=\"http://lm.int\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://lm.int&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792467660000000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2jywar5vBwiGipli3tWaeB\">lm.int</a></span>, <span style=\"color:rgb(153,0,0);font-weight:bold\">function</span><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">x</span><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">)</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">coef</span><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">x</span><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">)</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">)</span><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">)</span>, <span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">ncol</span><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,153,153)\">2</span>, <span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">byrow</span><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(153,0,115)\">T</span><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">)</span></code></pre><pre style=\"overflow:auto;font-size:13px;padding:9.5px;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:10px;line-height:1.42857;color:rgb(51,51,51);word-wrap:break-word;border:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);border-radius:4px\"><code style=\"font-size:inherit;padding:0px;color:inherit;border-radius:0px;white-space:pre-wrap;background-color:transparent\">##            [,1]       [,2]\r\n## [1,]   36.56873 -0.3212541\r\n## [2,]   40.44535 -0.3415142\r\n## [3,]   35.83966 -0.3144279\r\n## [4,]   22.58533 -0.2415899\r\n## [5,] -332.85617  1.7207225\r\n## [6,]   33.40853 -0.2964758</code></pre></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\">I hope the helps some. </div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\">-Matt</div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br clear=\"all\"><div><div class=\"gmail_signature\"><div dir=\"ltr\">______________________________<br><br>Matt Whalen<br>PhD Candidate, Ecology Graduate Group<br><span style=\"color:black\"><span>Department of Evolution &amp; Ecology<br></span>\r\n<span></span></span>University of California, Davis<br><font color=\"#000000\">Bodega Marine Laboratory</font><div><font color=\"#000000\">PO Box 247</font></div><div><font color=\"#000000\">Bodega Bay, CA 94923<br></font><div><font color=\"#000000\"><a href=\"http://mattwhalen.wordpress.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://mattwhalen.wordpress.com&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792467660000000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2yNgK8DF450WhZ81_ciUQo\">mattwhalen.wordpress.com</a><br></font>______________________________<br><br><br></div></div></div></div></div>\r\n<br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Thu, Dec 3, 2015 at 4:08 PM, Alex Webster <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">alx.w...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left-width:1px;border-left-color:rgb(204,204,204);border-left-style:solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">I find coplots a super useful visual tool for interpreting interactions in mixed models, but sometimes I&#39;d like to also see the breakdown in numbers so that I can compare intercepts, etc and know the exact bins of the &quot;Given&quot; variable that R is magically choosing. Does anyone know how to extract the regression output from coplots?<div><br><div>for example, this code below gives me the attached plot. I&#39;d be down to see the regression output for simple linear regressions if that&#39;s all I can get, or for the full mixed models at these different levels of the &quot;Given&quot; variable if possible. I realize that I could code the model for each of these different levels, but I&#39;d rather see what the coplot is doing and have them line up exactly. And it would be faster if there is just a line of code for this. Can&#39;t find anything via google, though others have asked the question, to no avail. Let me know what you think - Thanks!</div><div><br></div><div>coplot(log_DEA ~ daub_veg_H1_total_veg_cover | Fore_slope_ammended, rows=1, panel=panel.car, lowess.line=FALSE, data=DEAslope)<br></div><div><br></div><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"><a href=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-0yyz5iT4_5U/VmDXop_xOuI/AAAAAAAAPWs/IsQy7vvvJ68/s1600/Rplot.png\" style=\"margin-left:1em;margin-right:1em\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-0yyz5iT4_5U/VmDXop_xOuI/AAAAAAAAPWs/IsQy7vvvJ68/s1600/Rplot.png&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792467660000000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0gDT159pbS0IVtFzJpdx9l\"><img src=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-0yyz5iT4_5U/VmDXop_xOuI/AAAAAAAAPWs/IsQy7vvvJ68/s320/Rplot.png\" border=\"0\" width=\"320\" height=\"267\"></a></p></div></div></blockquote></div></div></div>"
    ],
